[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: The node-type migration proceeds now, with WORK as a type, without waiting for beads

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[DECISION]
UID: DEC-MIGRATE-BEFORE-BEADS
TITLE: The node-type migration proceeds now, with WORK as a type, without waiting for beads
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATUS: accepted
RETIRES_ON: Beads runs and takes WORK nodes themselves, not only their state, out of the canon.
STATEMENT: >>>
The node-type migration proceeds now, and WORK is a node type.
MECH-GRID-MIGRATION-UNCOSTED had gated it on DEC-PLAN-LIFECYCLE-OPEN, on the
argument that if execution lives in beads then work and probes might leave the
canon rather than become WORK. The operator ruled on 2026-08-30 that the
migration does not wait: probes become WORK when unrun and EVIDENCE when run;
beads, when it runs, may take execution STATE out of the canon, but not the
WORK nodes that declare what is to be built and what it crosses. What DEPTH
means on a WORK node -- design maturity or delivery -- stays open as
DEC-WORK-STATE-FIELD.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The operator's words: "the migration was the one question I care to answer" and
"beads isn't ready yet, which is fine". Waiting on beads to decide the shape of
work items delayed every ruling that depends on the vocabulary being spelled.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Ruled by the operator in conversation on 2026-08-30. AUTHORED_BY reads llm
because the writer has no flag for it -- the relayed-ruling gap the whiteboard
names. This decision lifts the gate; it does not supersede
DEC-PLAN-LIFECYCLE-OPEN, which stays open on retention.
<<<
